# Jog rate, in mm/s, and it is GLOBAL - LinuxCNC has one jog slider for all
# axes, not a per-axis rate. DEFAULT is where the slider starts; MAX is how
# far it can be pushed. Held at 1000 mm/min = 16.666667 mm/s on 2026-09-03,
# down from 1150 (and 50 mm/s before that): a high ceiling let Y and Z rapid at
# full speed while X clamped itself to its own 25 mm/s, and the jog was faster
# than wanted on the machine. DEFAULT is pinned to MAX so the slider starts at
# the travel speed actually asked for and cannot be pushed past it.
